#: projects/k3bmixedburndialog.cpp:149
msgid ""
"<p><b>Standard mixed mode CD 1</b><p>K3b will write the data track before all "
"audio tracks.<p>This mode should only be used for CDs that are unlikely to be "
"played on a hifi audio CD player.<p><b>Caution:</b> It could lead to problems "
"with some older hifi audio CD players that try to play the data track."
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bmixedburndialog.cpp:157
msgid "Last track will contain the data"
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bmixedburndialog.cpp:158
msgid ""
"<p><b>Standard mixed mode CD 2</b><p>K3b will write the data track after all "
"audio tracks.<p>This mode should only be used for CDs that are unlikely to be "
"played on a hifi audio CD player.<p><b>Caution:</b> It could lead to problems "
"with some older hifi audio CD players that try to play the data track."
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bmixedburndialog.cpp:166
msgid "The data will be written in a second session"
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bmixedburndialog.cpp:167
msgid ""
"<p><b>Blue book CD</b><p>K3b will create a multisession CD with 2 sessions. The "
"first session will contain all audio tracks and the second session will contain "
"a mode 2 form 1 data track.<p>This mode is based on the <em>Blue book</em> "
"standard (also known as <em>Extended Audio CD</em>, <em>CD-Extra</em>, or <em>"
"CD Plus</em>) and has the advantage that a hifi audio CD player will only "
"recognize the first session and ignore the second session with the data "
"track.<p>If the CD is intended to be used in a hifi audio CD player this is the "
"recommended mode.<p>Some older CD-ROMs may have problems reading a blue book CD "
"since it is a multisession CD."
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bdvdburndialog.cpp:53
msgid "DVD Project"
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bdvdburndialog.cpp:117
msgid ""
"<p>For DVD-R(W) in sequential incremental mode and DVD+R it behaves like "
"multisession CDs.<br> <b>Caution:</b> Most DVD-ROM drives are only able to read "
"the first session and most likely even on DVD writers only the first session "
"will be mounted.</p><p>For DVD+RW and DVD-RW in restricted overwrite mode K3b "
"will utilize growisofs to <em>grow</em> the ISO9660 filesystem in the first "
"session.</p><p><b>Be aware that K3b needs to write multisession DVDs "
"on-the-fly.</b>"
msgstr ""

#: projects/k3bdvdburndialog.cpp:225
msgid ""
"It is not possible to write multisession DVDs in DAO mode.Multisession has been "
"disabled."
